    "name": "Jalapeño Peppers",
    "description": "<p>Jalapeo peppers have a vegetal flavor similar to a green bell pepper and a front-of-mouth heat effect. The spiciness can vary widely among individual peppers. Jalapenos are picked green and generally used in this unripened state. Jalapenos turn red as they ripen, both on and off the plant. They usually fall in the range of 2,000 to 8,000 Scoville Heat Units (SHU), which sounds like a lot, but it really isn't!</p>",
